  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to accountability for human rights violations and to preparations for a credible reform process</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 18-month measure will, under a first component, provide support to the efforts of the Belarusian democratic movement to prepare for constitutional and electoral reform. This will include assistance for stakeholder consultations and for constitutional expertise. In a second component, the measure will help establish the International Accountability Platform for Belarus with a view to enable in-depth, transparent and impartial investigations into allegations of serious human rights violations in line with the recommendations made in November 2020 by the OSCE rapporteur, appointed by 17 OSCE participating States under the Moscow Mechanism. The Platform will build on the ongoing efforts to document human rights violations. Bringing together high-level expertise from a consortium of Belarusian and international non-governmental organisations, the Platform will enhance the quality and completeness of the documentation. The aim is to generate a body of impartial evidence to provide a basis for criminal investigations in accordance with international law standards. Through its two components, the measure will help prepare a basis for a peaceful and democratic transition once the circumstances allow and contribute to the global fight against impunity.</narrative>
  </description>
